# TDD Workflow

Every bug fix and every task from `tasks/` follows three **separate** turns unless the user
explicitly collapses them ("just do it", "implement now", or similar).

## Phase 1 — Red (test only)

Write or extend a test that captures the expected behaviour. **Do not change production code.**

- **Bug fix:** the test must reproduce the defect and **fail** against current code. Run it and
  show the failure before stopping.
- **Feature / task:** the test encodes the agreed contract from the spec (or the user's
  description if no spec yet). It may fail because the feature is missing — that is expected.

Stop after the test. Summarise what it asserts and what failed. Do not propose or implement a fix
in the same turn.

Test conventions: `.cursor/skills/relay-dev-workflow/SKILL.md` (§ Tests).

## Phase 2 — Diagnose and propose (no implementation)

Investigate root cause and recommend an approach. Follow
`.cursor/rules/challenge-proposed-solutions.mdc` — verify the diagnosis, weigh alternatives, ask
what blocks a decision. **Do not edit production code or make the test pass yet.**

**Create or update** `spec/<slug>.md` with the agreed direction: design, contracts, alternatives,
and **`## Contributions`** (user's proposal vs agent additions). See
`.cursor/rules/document-every-change.mdc`.

Stop with a concrete proposal and open questions. Wait for the user to agree, refine, or reject.

## Phase 3 — Green (implement after agreement)

Only after the user confirms the approach (or refines it and confirms again):

1. Implement the agreed fix or feature.
2. Run the Phase 1 test — it must **pass**.
3. Write the mandatory record per `.cursor/rules/document-every-change.mdc`.

If the agreed approach differs from what the test expects, update the test **with** the
implementation and say why.

## Boundaries

- One phase per user message by default. If the user sends a new bug or task, start at Phase 1
  even if the previous item is mid-flow.
- Phase 1 may include test helpers or fixtures; it must not include the fix.
- Phase 3 may include refactors needed for the agreed solution, not speculative clean-up.
- Trivial reversible changes (typo, rename, comment, log line) skip all three phases.

## What to say at the end of each phase

| Phase | Stop with |
|---|---|
| 1 | failing test output, what the test covers, "ready for diagnosis" |
| 2 | root cause, recommended approach, alternatives, questions, **`spec/<slug>.md` draft** — "ready to implement when you agree" |
| 3 | passing test output, files changed, pointer to **`docs/NNN-*.md`** and final **`spec/`** |
